cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "RoboECG: autonomous robotic placement of 12-lead ECG precordial electrodes in Isaac Sim"
abstract: >-
  Simulation study of a robot arm that perceives a supine patient's chest with an
  overhead depth camera, localises the six precordial ECG electrodes (V1-V6) from
  explicit clinical rules, presses them onto the skin and verifies its own work.
  The localisation rules are checked against two independently published electrode
  datasets (25 statistical-shape torso models; PhysioNet/CinC 2007 case 3).
type: software
